<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb refined copper output rises 0.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb refined copper output rises 0.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese refined copper output in February rose a seasonally adjusted 0.3 percent from the prior month, according to Ministry of International Trade and Industry data released on Friday.</p>
<p>On an unadjusted basis, output was off 0.1 percent year-on-year at 99,887 tonnes.</p>
<p>The February data was as follows (in tonnes, percent):</p>
<p>		 Feb 97     Jan 97   y/y change  s/a change*</p>
<p> Output	99,887    105,747     - 0.1	 + 0.3</p>
<p> Shipments  102,578    104,061     - 2.9	 - 4.6</p>
<p> Stocks	48,769     52,118     - 2.7	 + 7.0</p>
<p>(*Seasonally adjusted change, month-on-month)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
